WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:01.930
My lady!

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:06.730
So what is the real reason the suspect 
threw the corpse into this swamp?

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.820
It was so the suspect, Tanio Aoi,

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.280
could have the police find something 
that she was looking for.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.130
She had previously tossed 
something away in this swamp,

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.820
and after murdering Yoshihara Hiroo,

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.450
she figured she should retrieve it.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:23.710
But it was quite impossible for her to find

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.460
what she had thrown into 
this swamp all on her own.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:29.460
That's why she decided 
to get the police to help.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.050
If she told them she had dumped 
the murder weapon here,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.790
there's a good chance the police 
would've searched the swamp.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.030
Then what about the thing she whispered?

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.390
It wasn't a dead body she wanted them to find.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:43.450
It was something she had 
tossed into the swamp before.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.480
Though she tossed it in quite a while ago,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:48.410
so there was no guarantee that it'd be found.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.950
That's why she couldn't stop 
herself from whispering a prayer.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:56.210
I really hope they find you.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:01.990
That was the whisper that you heard.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.730
Then she didn't need to 
go through the trouble

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.210
of bringing the corpse here.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:39.130
She could have just said 
the murder weapon was here.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:42.230
But that brings up some inconsistencies.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.510
To carry out her plan, 
Tanio Aoi needed the police

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:47.280
to find out about the incident,

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.520
believe that she was the 
culprit and arrest her,

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.020
and hear her confess that she threw 
the murder weapon into the swamp.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.290
So first, how would she get the police 
to find out about the incident?

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.090
They'd have to find the body.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.660
Precisely, Kuro-san!

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:05.120
And how would she go about doing that?

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.390
Well...

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.120
Should she confess immediately? 
Of course not.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.030
The fact that she threw 
the weapon into the swamp

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.570
would mean she was trying 
to conceal the crime.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:16.050
And a suspect like that wouldn't 
admit to their crimes.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.250
Exactly.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.270
Many hikers come through here,

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.470
so the body would've been discovered quickly.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:23.340
And she mentioned during her interrogation

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.770
that she wanted the giant 
serpent to eat the body.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:30.100
That should cause the police to question 
her sanity and work even harder

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.930
on the investigation to discover the truth.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.350
So what is that woman trying 
to get them to find?

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:39.860
What do you believe she threw 
into the swamp long ago?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.210
I'm sure it was something that had to do with

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:44.530
her former boyfriend, Machii Yoshikazu-san.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:49.290
I'm sure she must have resented him 
after the incident five years ago.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.040
But this was all set up by Yoshihara Hiroo.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.990
She found out her boyfriend was innocent.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:56.150
It can be presumed that

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.800
Tanio Aoi very much regretted 
the fact that she doubted him.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:03.210
I see. It makes sense that she would 
want to get rid of any reminders

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.760
of the man who betrayed her.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.680
But now, she was trying to retrieve it.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:13.460
Isn't this all rather dramatic just to 
reclaim a single item she had lost?

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.900
Absolutely.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.020
After the incident with her boyfriend,

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:20.950
she had returned home from 
living alone in the city.

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:25.450
She probably got rid of most items related 
to her boyfriend during her move.

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.970
Even if she had kept a couple 
of pictures and presents,

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:31.480
she could have just thrown them 
in the trash or burned them.

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:35.090
Then what are you saying that 
she threw into the swamp?

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:41.910
Well...

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:45.260
Perhaps it was a baby she 
had with her boyfriend.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:53.060
Shortly after her boyfriend's death and 
subsequently moving back home,

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:55.230
Aoi realized that she 
was pregnant with his child.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.850
Because she didn't know 
the truth at the time,

00:04:57.850 --> 00:04:59.940
she saw it as the child of 
the man who betrayed her.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:02.430
Despite the child being blameless,

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.240
she likely still wondered 
what she should do.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.990
But then, one day,

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:10.580
she ended up having a miscarriage at home,

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.910
and the corpse of the fetus 
ended up in her hands.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:16.540
I'm sure she was troubled 
over how to dispose of it.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:20.210
Unable to tell anyone about it, 
she dealt with it all alone.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:26.010
And then, last month, she found out 
the truth about her boyfriend's death

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:28.380
and regretted her actions even further.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.140
She figured she should probably

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.930
try to find the fetus and 
give it a proper burial.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.810
That's why she thought up the plan 
to have the police search the swamp.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:43.810
So you're saying that that woman's 
dead infant would eventually be found?

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.430
I doubt that it will.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:48.300
You just said yourself

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.660
that you regularly have this swamp cleaned.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:57.690
It's most likely that her baby sank 
into the swamp about four years ago.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:01.340
So the mountain ayakashi 
probably pulled it out long ago.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.720
Tanio Aoi tossed a tiny 
corpse into the swamp.

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:11.430
I'm sure she came up these mountains 
alone one night so she wouldn't be found.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:16.270
That's what made her think to dispose 
of the man's body at night the same way.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.890
By throwing that corpse into the swamp,

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:22.480
she wanted to retrieve the precious 
little corpse she had lost.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.990
This explanation doesn't 
contradict anything you said

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.700
and seems the most plausible.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:37.470
Humans truly think up and 
commit such horrendous acts.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:38.870
Indeed, they do.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:41.930
I'd say you're also slightly 
terrifying, my lady,

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:43.630
but there's something even more...

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.460
Oh, how simply frightful!

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.430
Beware of
mountain
fires

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.430
Was that deduction really true?

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.720
A dead baby? Really?

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:59.310
What I do know is that everything 
Tanio Aoi told the police was not a lie,

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:03.440
and apparently, she really did want 
the Guardian to eat the corpse.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.790
Before meeting with the Guardian,

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:10.240
I had a ghost visit Tanio Aoi 
in her holding cell...

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:13.820
Did the serpent not find the body?

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.950
And the ghost heard her say that.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.660
So you knew that and lined 
up one lie after another.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.630
Indeed, I did.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:26.780
Even still, my explanation made 
sense and seemed reasonable.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:31.110
But there's no guarantee that 
the suspect would act rationally.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:36.000
The Guardian had said that if she 
wanted them to eat the corpse,

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.320
she would've just said so.

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:41.410
But for her, nothing would start 
until they found the body,

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.100
which is why she whispered that.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:46.310
I believe that's quite possible.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:51.780
This may be going too far, but there is 
also the possibility that the Guardian

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.410
misheard what she whispered.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:56.810
That would completely destroy 
the original premise.

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:00.220
And a great yokai who's 
renowned as the Guardian

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:02.090
would never admit to mishearing someone.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:05.900
Correct. That's why I used some of my wisdom.

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.240
I think I understand your true powers now.

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.840
But still, you should be more cautious 
about the danger you put yourself in.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.180
And I wouldn't have to worry about that 
if you would just stay by my side...

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.070
You never mentioned helping you

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:22.780
exterminate yokai as a condition 
for going out with you.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:25.060
So you admit that we're dating, then.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.050
I did not.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:44.000
<b>The Rumors of the Steel Lady</b>

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.690
<b>Two years later</b>

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:54.490
So, yeah. The new girl at work is super cute.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:57.010
Also, they were pretty huge.

00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.510
What? What am I talking about?

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:01.140
Her boobs...

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.220
are huge...

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:17.410
Hey, Yumihara.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:18.570
Yes?

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.570
The other day, when I 
invited you out for yakiniku,

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:23.450
you declined, saying that eating beef

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:27.000
reminds you of an ex-boyfriend 
you had a nasty falling-out with

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.440
and makes you feel sick.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:31.210
So why are you eating the 
kalbi lunch right now?

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:34.210
I realized I shouldn't let 
the past hold me back,

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.410
so I'm doing everything I can to get over it.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.340
I see...

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.010
Well, when you get over it, let me know.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:41.810
I'll invite you out for yakiniku again.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.450
By the way, you handled

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.980
the report for the accident by 
Makuragawa River three days ago, right?

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:46.690
Yes.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:48.340
The report says the young man

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:50.630
thought he saw a puppy 
jump out in front of him,

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:54.150
so he panicked drove through 
the guardrail into the river.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:57.800
But I heard he had a different story at first.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.100
That statement was taken when 
he had just been pulled

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.120
out of the river in a hysterical state.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:06.230
Once he calmed down, he confirmed 
that was not actually the case.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:09.630
So it's true that this 
college student initially said...

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.630
that a girl wielding a steel 
beam about two meters long,

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:16.380
who was wearing a flashy, frilly 
red and black dress

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:19.840
and a huge bow in her hair,
but who somehow had no face,

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.890
suddenly appeared in front of his car, 
so he panicked and swerved off the road.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.120
He did say that?

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:27.110
Yes.

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.770
Then why did you use the 
statement regarding the puppy?

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:33.930
Because it doesn't matter if it was 
a puppy or a ghost that popped out.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:35.460
They're pretty different...

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:36.780
Terada-san...

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:40.030
Are you looking for Steel Lady Nanase?

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.170
Steel Lady Nanase?

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:43.700
You've never heard of her?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.190
Then have you heard of Nanase Karin?

00:10:45.190 --> 00:10:46.750
Oh, isn't she...

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.670
the idol who died at the 
beginning of this year?

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:53.000
I remember hearing the media was abuzz 
over her due to some unsavory rumors.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.460
Yup.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.590
And to get away from the media,

00:10:56.590 --> 00:10:59.420
she holed up in a hotel 
here in Makurazaka City,

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:03.660
but then she died when a steel beam 
from a nearby construction site fell on her.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.660
Warning

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.760
I heard she had a huge rack.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.490
But there are rumors 
swirling about her again.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:10.630
What? Like it was suicide after all?

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:11.400
No...

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.370
It seems...

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.610
she appears every night in Makurazaka City.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:19.420
She's even wearing her outfit 
from when she was an idol,

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:22.180
and wielding the steel beam that crushed her...

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:25.580
The faceless ghost of Nanase Karin.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:27.450
And what do you think about all that?

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:31.890
I decided it wasn't the best idea to leave 
any stories about a ghost in writing.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:33.940
That's not the point I'm talking about.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.500
I want to know how you feel about this.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:38.840
Do you really think a ghost or monster

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:41.390
named "Steel Lady Nanase" is really out there?

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:45.810
The college student's terrified face,

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:48.220
the tire tracks and the guardrail 
that was busted through,

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:50.220
and...

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:56.580
that eerie feeling I felt lingering in 
the air there... they were all real.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:00.970
I do believe that the college 
student really saw something

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:02.630
that shouldn't have been there.

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:09.040
Police boxes around the city have 
had people claiming that they saw

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:12.550
or were nearly attacked by someone 
resembling Steel Lady Nanase.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:15.170
They're actually reporting it at police boxes?

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:20.260
The police there are shrugging it off by 
saying they were all just seeing things,

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.220
but ever since the middle of last month,

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.260
cases involving random attacks

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:27.720
and assault attempts have been 
on the rise throughout the city.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:29.100
Terada-san.

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.390
Do you honestly believe 
that Steel Lady Nanase

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:34.100
actually exists and is attacking people?

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:40.600
Hey, come on, now. 
Don't make me sound crazy.

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:42.320
Of course I don't believe in ghosts.

00:12:42.850 --> 00:12:45.260
I'm sure this is the work of the living.

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:50.660
If someone is truly appearing in 
various locations dressed like that,

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:53.910
it seems like a lot of trouble for a mere 
prankster or kidnapper to go through.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.080
That's the part that bugs me, too.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:59.620
If it's necessary at all to 
go through all that trouble,

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:03.290
there must be a significant reason 
or objective behind this.

00:13:04.070 --> 00:13:07.260
Something that's not just a 
prank, but an actual crime.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:12.850
These reports started happening within 
the city over the past two weeks.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.850
Do not use
these relationship sites!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.850
<b>It could even be this man!!</b>

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.850
<b>We're waiting for
your help to
protect this city
Looking for
police officers</b>

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.850
Let's all protect
this city together

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:16.560
We started seeing more information 
on the Internet around then, too.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:16.560
An accident occurred in which a college student crashed 
into the guardrail and plunged into the river.

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:20.980
They've had from when the rumors started 
spreading until two weeks ago to prepare.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:24.820
And more recently, they finally 
started making their move.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:29.070
It looks bad for a police officer 
to take rumors like this seriously.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:32.700
But there's definitely something.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:37.890
Right now, the suburbs are a 
hotbed for organized crime.

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:40.710
Meaning someone should 
definitely keep an eye out.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.750
<i>Terada-san believes the 
emergence of Steel Lady Nanase</i>

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:46.110
<i>is foreshadowing a much bigger crime.</i>

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:47.300
<i>But...</i>

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.930
<i>Steel Lady Nanase is definitely real.</i>

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:54.280
<i>She's a real ghost that has nothing 
to do with some other crime or plot.</i>

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:56.060
<i>No matter what may happen in the future,</i>

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.330
<i>the police won't be able to deal with her.</i>

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:02.620
It'd be great if you'd be willing to help out.

00:14:02.620 --> 00:14:03.480
Terada-san.

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.990
Please just remember this.

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:11.070
There is a possibility that yokai and 
ghosts actually exist in this world.

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:16.350
Really, Yumihara? 
You believe in stuff like that?

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:18.460
I haven't seen any ghosts,

00:14:18.860 --> 00:14:21.330
but I have seen yokai before.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.540
What are you talking about?

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.780
If you don't believe it's possible 
that there are beings

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:28.840
that surpass all logic and 
reasoning in this world,

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:30.720
you're going to be blindsided one day.

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:31.850
Right...

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:34.770
<i>I'm sure there's no point 
in saying any of this.</i>

00:14:36.420 --> 00:14:38.760
Because I didn't believe that was the case,

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:41.020
I ended up having to break up with my ex.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:46.350
Oh, uh... So was your ex a yokai or a ghost?

00:14:58.620 --> 00:14:59.340
Excuse me.

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:00.710
Hey, Yumihara!

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:14.470
I guess you really do feel 
sick after eating meat.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.690
Want me to bring you some water?

00:15:16.690 --> 00:15:18.700
No, I'm fine, thank you.

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:19.980
As I was saying, Terada-san,

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:23.990
there are beings that surpass 
our logic and reasoning.

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:25.690
Please, just be careful.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.690
All right, I got it.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:31.530
At least, I get the fact that you 
were in a complicated relationship.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:35.700
Um... It just ended up complicated.

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:38.450
Well, see you later. I'm counting on you.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:47.890
Kuro-kun!

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:55.100
Humans are so terrifying...

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:59.850
You will consume anything and are 
willing to mix with anything.

00:15:59.850 --> 00:16:02.770
They create monsters like you...

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:05.020
How terrifying!

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:14.340
<i>That monster happened to be my fiancé,</i>

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:17.780
<i>and there'd come a day when I'd seriously 
have to consider how I could stay with him.</i>

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:19.940
Kuro-kun?

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:22.620
Saki-san.

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:26.780
<i>How could I ever have imagined it?</i>

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:30.510
<i>Ever since that day,</i>

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:33.320
<i>the world that I once 
believed in became warped,</i>

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:35.640
<i>and the more I lived my life in fear,</i>

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:39.390
<i>the more I sensed the presence 
of those creatures.</i>

00:16:40.030 --> 00:16:43.230
<i>I wonder how long this life of gloom 
and doom is going to continue.</i>

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:49.150
<i>Even this hill that I climb 
every day makes me worry.</i>

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:57.280
Whoa... Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:16:58.110 --> 00:16:58.990
<i>A girl?</i>

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:05.130
Are you all right?

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:05.870
Yes.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:08.460
This is nothing compared to being deflowered.

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:12.490
Why in the world would you bring up such 
a graphic example at a time like this?!

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:13.840
Well, I mean...

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.340
It was the most painful experience 
of my life. Can you blame me?

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:21.270
Upsy-daisy.

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:24.230
<i>Kids these days sure come 
up with some bizarre jokes.</i>

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:28.150
<i>Is she actually a child? 
Wait, just how old is she?</i>

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:32.110
I'm not sure who you are, 
but thank you very much.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:34.770
<i>She's rather petite and cute.</i>

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:35.400
<i>But...</i>

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.450
<i>What's this strange 
presence I sense from her?</i>

00:17:39.690 --> 00:17:42.290
I realize that you were kind 
enough to save me,

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.410
but please take my advice and run away.

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.430
From what?

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:02.940
Steel Lady... Nanase!

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:03.990
Please, run away.

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:05.890
Your eyes aren't playing tricks on you.

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.170
She's exactly what she seems to be.

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.760
A creature that's often referred 
to as a spirit, monster, or yokai.

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:15.070
I know... That presence is real.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:17.500
Those giant boobs are real, too.

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.740
Is that really relevant right now?!

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:24.230
Enough.

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:25.580
I'm done with this.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:32.540
<i>I ran away from the kappa, 
ran away from Kuro-kun...</i>

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:35.340
<i>And I'm living a life of 
depression because of it.</i>

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:39.680
<i>I'm sick of letting these things rule my life!</i>

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:41.970
<i>All this absurdity...</i>

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:44.760
<i>I'm going to be done with it tonight!</i>

00:18:58.570 --> 00:18:59.950
<i>This is...</i>

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:01.710
<i>illogical.</i>

00:19:01.710 --> 00:19:04.080
This is why I told you to run away!

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.650
Whoa, whoa...

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:59.150
She fled...

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:02.290
I won't be able to defeat that 
thing with brute force, though.

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:06.550
<i>I don't know what's going on.</i>

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:08.850
<i>She just kicked a ghost.</i>

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:11.060
<i>Who in the world is she?</i>

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:14.580
<i>Wait, is she not human, either?</i>

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.670
Have no fear. It's a prosthetic.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:20.690
It's built to come off 
if it gets overburdened.

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:24.360
Because if it doesn't come off, 
I could harm myself even more.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:28.090
Why were you able to touch 
that thing when I wasn't?

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:31.150
Are you like a yokai, as well?

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:33.000
Oh... No.

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:36.450
I'm somewhere in between...

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:41.460
I don't know who you are, 
and I see that you're a brave soul,

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.800
but please forget everything you saw today.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:47.510
I'll take care of Steel Lady 
Nanase in the very near future.

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:50.430
That's the reason I'm here.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.980
I'd rather not get the police involved,

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.350
so please don't tell anyone about me, either.

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.450
You can tell me more back at the station. 
It's right at the bottom of this hill.

00:21:01.980 --> 00:21:02.960
Unbelievable!

00:21:02.960 --> 00:21:06.930
Your leg might be okay, but I'm sure 
you have bruises and cuts everywhere.

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:08.070
I'll treat them for you.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:09.860
Don't worry.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:13.830
Traffic Division

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:13.830
I don't plan to get a statement from 
you or try to contact your family.

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:15.620
But there are incidents

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.750
that the police believe Steel Lady 
Nanase is responsible for,

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.780
so I can't just let this go.

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:24.760
A police officer from the traffic 
division, Yumihara Saki...

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.770
Are you actually Saki-san?!

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:32.520
Um... I'm not sure what 
you're talking abou—

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:37.420
Your hair is shorter, and you 
may have lost some weight...

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:39.900
That's why I didn't realize it!

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:43.560
Augh! I never would've saved you 
if I knew you were Saki-san!

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.400
I mean, I wouldn't just let you die, but...

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:49.420
Explain this in a way I can understand.

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:50.980
Do you know me?

00:21:52.220 --> 00:21:54.620
I don't recall us ever meeting before.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:59.250
We have met before, but this is the first 
time we've properly greeted each other.

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:01.760
My name is Iwanaga Kotoko.

00:22:01.760 --> 00:22:04.760
I'm Sakuragawa Kuro-senpai's 
current girlfriend!

00:22:10.260 --> 00:22:11.450
Meep!

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:16.330
To Be Continued

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:46.980
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:47.740
Steel Lady Nanase strikes with violence.

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:51.700
Her original form, the idol Nanase Karin, 
died a mysterious death.

00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:53.160
To defeat Steel Lady Nanase,

00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:56.560
we'll have to find out the truth 
behind Nanase Karin's death.

00:23:56.560 --> 00:23:59.500
Next time, "Idol Dies by Steel Beam."
